            <value>
               <exData contentType="text/html">
                  <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/"><p style="text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:0in">The GSTG amount is determined based on your estimated Cost of Attendance (COA), minus other Financial Aid awarded.<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span></p><ul style="text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:0in;list-style-type:disc"><li>COA includes tuition and fees, room and board, books and supplies, transportation, and miscellaneous expenses.<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span></li><li>To maximize the amount of GSTG this academic year, you have the option to<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span><span style="font-weight:bold">request a reduction or cancelation of student loan(s)</span> you may have accepted or received. This means that GSTG funds will replace the loans, essentially paying off a portion or the entirety of your loans for the Academic Year or semester.<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span></li><li>Review our Financial Aid website for more information on how Middle Class Scholarship is affected by GSTG and how the Federal TEACH grant impacts eligibility for the GSTG funds.</li></ul></body>
