                     <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/"><p style="text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:0in">The Golden State Teacher Grant(GSTG) is state funding offered by the California Student Aid Commission (CSAC) for students enrolled in a teaching credential program. The online GSTG CSAC application deadline is April 1, 2025, and must be submitted if you’re a new applicant for this program. Submit this form every new academic year to have your GSTG eligibility reviewed by our office, deadline<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span><span style="font-weight:bold">May 16, 2025</span>. Applications are processed after Census date (typically the fifth week of the semester); submissions after Census will be processed in 2-3 weeks.<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span></p><p style="text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:0in">GSTG program can pay up to $20,000, distributed throughout multiple academic years; however, you must complete the credential program within three years from the date the first payment is disbursed to you. Please review<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span><a href="https://www.csac.ca.gov/gstg">CSAC’s website</a> for additional information, and our<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span><a href="https://www.fullerton.edu/financialaid/graduate/goldenstateteachergrant.php">Financial Aid website</a> for the application process.</p></body>
